/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Board-level Early Detection of Risk Committee which was established in 2010 acts as an advisory committee to the Board of Directors in terms of early detection of financial and operational risks. The Early Detection of Risk Committee is the highest governing body for the oversight of all risks and opportunities of the Company. Thus, governing and evaluating sustainability-related risks and opportunities including climate-related ones falls under the responsibility of this committee. Additionally, once sustainability and climate-related risk and opportunity items are qualitatively and quantitatively evaluated, action plans and related investment needs are carefully laid out by each team involved in the process. Such risks are discussed at the Sustainability Council to inform the C-level and D-level and reported to the Early Detection of Risk Committee with the help of the Enterprise Risk and Insurance Management Department. To manage and mitigate the risks, action plans are taken into consideration.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
