<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The packaging risk associated with upcoming regulations and potential taxes on recycled content is an emerging concern for manufacturers. As governments in regions like the UK and Spain implement plastic packaging taxes targeting low recycled plastic content, companies face rising costs. Additionally, fluctuations in the price, quality, and durability of recycled plastic raw materials add complexity to supply chains. These factors drive the need for innovation in packaging design and material sourcing. Manufacturers must proactively adapt to evolving regulatory landscapes to mitigate financial impact and maintain competitiveness. This emerging risk highlights the growing importance of sustainable packaging strategies in reducing environmental impact while managing cost pressures.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
